WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:10.920
About 12 years ago
I met a beautiful girl.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.600
I fell head over heels in love.

3
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.400
The girl and her friend
had just come up with a plan

4
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.440
to go to Australia for a year.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.720
I thought it's a great plan,
let's meet in a year,

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.240
but when I was seeing them off
at the airport,

7
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:28.960
I realized that I wanted to spend
this year in Australia too.

8
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.560
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

9
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.360
BECAUSE OF LOVE

10
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.880
That year of enjoying the local culture
on a working holiday visa

11
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.280
turned into another year and then into

12
00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.280
a year and a half in New Zealand.

13
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.680
Finally, we arrived in Canada.

14
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.120
We ended up working
at a very adventurous place,

15
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.400
that does heli-skiing in the winter.

16
00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:10.720
While sitting on the slopes
of the ski hill on our free days,

17
00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.920
we noticed that there were
so many young families

18
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.920
with their 1-2-3-5 year old children

19
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.080
who skied much better
than we ever could.

20
00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:26.640
I had this feeling that
I wanted that too.

21
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:31.120
I want to have
such awesome kids someday

22
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:38.960
who spend their youth on the slopes,
laughing and having fun.

23
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.120
Now, six years later,
we're almost there,

24
00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.360
in a few months we'll have
our first child.

25
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.760
I can't wait for us to start pushing

26
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:58.160
this little toddler
up the slopes together.

27
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:08.720
I met my current partner and the father
of my child by chance in Tallinn.

28
00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:12.120
It was love at first sight.

29
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:17.320
Six months after we met,
I moved to Switzerland.

30
00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.280
Nothing was holding me back in Estonia,

31
00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:23.040
and it seemed
like an exciting challenge.

32
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.880
When I left Estonia,

33
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.120
I had quite a few relationships
that had gone bad in a row.

34
00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.880
It was really interesting that
when I came to England,

35
00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:39.000
several things happened at once.

36
00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:45.920
I went to my first job interview
in early January.

37
00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:55.120
A few weeks before that, I was using
the popular dating app Tinder.

38
00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:02.080
I met or matched
with a young man there,

39
00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.160
and we started talking.

40
00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:10.920
Our communication went well right away,
maybe from the first moment.

41
00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.400
I felt some kind of connection.

42
00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:19.680
I mentioned to him that I was coming
to England in a couple of weeks.

43
00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:25.760
We first met in Manchester,
in the north of England.

44
00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:29.920
He came from London to meet me.

45
00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.360
I had a job interview that same day.

46
00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:36.680
I got a call right after that
and they said I got the job.

47
00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:41.320
That same night, I also had my
first date with my current partner.

48
00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:52.240
My new partner had a job opportunity
at the European Parliament.

49
00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:57.480
I moved to Brussels with him.

50
00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:04.120
But we didn't stay together.

51
00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:08.960
I went to work
in a big sports pub in Brussels,

52
00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:13.560
where I met my current husband.

53
00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:18.880
We've been married for a few weeks now.

54
00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:27.280
He's from Türkiye.
He's actually Kurdish.

55
00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.880
During the Covid pandemic,
the pub in Brussels was closed,

56
00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:36.600
the one we both worked at.

57
00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:42.280
I had a new job opportunity
at the time.

58
00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.200
That I could work from home.

59
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.600
Then we decided to come to live
in Türkiye, in Istanbul,

60
00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:54.720
where my husband's parents
and the whole family live.

61
00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:59.840
And we have settled in here for now.

62
00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.680
I would definitely get paid more
in my profession in Estonia.

63
00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:18.320
That's for sure.

64
00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:23.160
But there are other
positive things here.

65
00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:28.760
I can't just think about money.
We can't just think about salary.

66
00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:37.160
I truly believe that
I have the best relationship

67
00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.600
I've ever seen in anyone's life,

68
00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:44.360
whether it's friends, acquaintances,
or even celebrities.

69
00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.680
I really think I have the best
relationship than anyone else.

70
00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:52.800
And I wouldn't be willing
to sacrifice that for anything.

71
00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:56.000
When we went to sign
the marriage papers,

72
00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:00.520
they already prepared a form for me
saying I would become Portuguese.

73
00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.800
I said no,
I don't want to become Portuguese.

74
00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.000
I'm not changing my nationality
when I get married.

75
00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:12.120
Then they were like, why then?
Why don't you want to be Portuguese?

76
00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.120
Why do you prefer to be Estonian?

77
00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:18.080
It came to them
like a bolt from the blue.

78
00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.400
Isn't it better to be Portuguese?

79
00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.760
The thing is, they always think

80
00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:27.280
that I'm here looking for
better living conditions. Always!

81
00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.000
I'm not here
for better living conditions,

82
00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:33.680
I'm only here for my husband.

83
00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.520
If you say you're an immigrant
in America, everyone thinks

84
00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.360
you're an economic immigrant.
Life was bad in Estonia,

85
00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.280
so I came to America to live
a good life and earn money.

86
00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.400
Like builders who go to Finland.

87
00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.560
That is not the case with me,
I am there for love.

88
00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:02.920
I never planned to go to America.

89
00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.840
This is annoying,
I have to explain it again.

90
00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:09.480
Same goes for the question
of where Estonia is located.

91
00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:12.960
I say it's somewhere between
Suriname and Mongolia.

92
00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:15.440
They then say, "Yes, of course I know!"

93
00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.280
And then I grin.

94
00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:20.840
I've gotten a little impatient with it,

95
00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.440
no point in explaining,
they don't care anyway.

96
00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.560
Kui küsiti, kas mul on tüdruksõber,
siis vastasin lihtsalt ei.

97
00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.120
Ja see oli kõigile piisav vastus.

98
00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:43.920
Ma ei osanud arvatagi,
et see oleks probleem.

99
00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:51.440
Siis otsustasin kõigiga avameelne olla
ja see sundis mind linnast lahkuma.

100
00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:55.520
Ma tundsin lihtsalt...

101
00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:01.280
peaaegu vastikust selle pärast,
mida inimesed sellest arvavad.

102
00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:06.640
Niisiis kolisin Tallinna,
kus elab mu ema.

103
00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.240
Ja sellega oli jälle teine lugu.

104
00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:16.000
Sest kui Narvas oli raske olla gei,

105
00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:19.360
siis Tallinnas oli raske,
kui sa ei osanud eesti keelt.

106
00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:31.280
Siis mõistsin,
et maailm on suurem kui Narva,

107
00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.320
suurem kui Eesti.

108
00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:38.320
Ja otsustasin parema elu nimel lahkuda.

109
00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:49.880
My self-definition has a very
strong influence on my decision

110
00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.680
not to return to Estonia.

111
00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.560
It's strongly linked to the fact that

112
00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:59.720
I don't want to be special
because I'm gay.

113
00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:03.800
That's the shortest way to explain it.

114
00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:08.920
I think it's still the case in Estonia
that if I expressed myself

115
00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.760
that this is my wife,
eyebrows would be raised.

116
00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:15.360
If I had a gay friend with me
who said that's my husband

117
00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.560
and pointed at the man,
eyebrows would be raised again.

118
00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.520
That doesn't interest me.

119
00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:25.640
It's actually very insignificant
in the bigger picture.

120
00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.000
There are still many people in Estonia

121
00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:31.720
who directly associate having a child
with a heterosexual relationship.

122
00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:33.080
Absurd!

123
00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:37.040
Living in such a society
is not interesting to me.

124
00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:41.320
I can't live my life.
I have to be placative.

125
00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:46.080
I have to fight for some things
that are completely secondary.

126
00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:51.640
Returning to Estonia versus my
orientation and self-definition

127
00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:54.120
are very strongly connected.

128
00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.200
So strongly connected that
I don't want to go back to Estonia,

129
00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.440
precisely because of how
I define myself.

130
00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.360
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

131
00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:06.000
BECAUSE OF LOVE

132
00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.640
Translated by / Tõlkinud
Piret Õunapuu, Film Tower
